# Board and stats presentation refinements

Refine the Board building treatment and the stats table introduced by TASK-055 and TASK-056.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Settlement and city icons remain inside white boxes.
- [x] Building icons have crisp black outer and internal edge lines, including White-player buildings and ghost placements.
- [x] Stats headers show each active player's colour name in that colour rather than a dot.
- [x] Longest Road is shown as a black road icon inside a golden circle beside an independently centred Road Length number.
- [x] The golden road badge retains TASK-055's hold, shake, lift, drag, valid tied transfer, and invalid-return behavior.
- [x] Expanding and collapsing stats moves the table, tab, and arrow coherently without fade/replacement artifacts.
- [x] Relevant UI regression coverage compiles.

## Evidence

- Restored white building tiles and strengthened the two-layer black/color symbol treatment.
- Replaced player dots with colored player-name headers.
- Replaced the crown artwork with a draggable golden road badge while preserving the existing half-second hold gesture and reassignment rules.
- Kept the stats table mounted and moved the table, tab, and rotating persistent arrow as one fixed-height group using a single 0.28-second animation transaction, with no opacity animation.
- Added a UI assertion for the named player header.
- `xcodebuild build -project HexIQ.xcodeproj -scheme HexIQ -destination 'generic/platform=iOS Simulator' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO` succeeded.

## Manual checks

- Inspect building inner outlines and the stats animation on a device at normal and larger Dynamic Type sizes.
- Exercise valid and invalid Longest Road drops to confirm the badge's visual return behavior.
